1
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:06,649
What's happened? The time vortex has
gone! We've got to be somewhere.

2
00:00:06,689 --> 00:00:10,204
It's a parallel Earth with
zeppelins. I'm right, aren't I?

3
00:00:10,244 --> 00:00:12,480
A world where my dad's still alive.

4
00:00:12,520 --> 00:00:15,358
Rose, he's not your father.
And she is not your mother.

5
00:00:15,398 --> 00:00:17,511
What is that?
Mickey, we've got power!

6
00:00:17,551 --> 00:00:20,983
You're a fine businessman, John.
But you're not God.

7
00:00:21,023 --> 00:00:23,940
He is exactly the same.

8
00:00:26,459 --> 00:00:28,176
What are they? Cybermen.

9
00:00:38,959 --> 00:00:41,076
There's no need to damage us!

10
00:00:41,116 --> 00:00:45,228
We're good stock. We volunteer
for the upgrade programme.

11
00:00:45,268 --> 00:00:49,462
Take us to be processed. You are
rogue elements. But we surrender.

12
00:00:49,502 --> 00:00:53,054
You are incompatible.
But this is a surrender!

13
00:00:53,094 --> 00:00:57,727
You will be deleted.
Listen to me, we surrender!

14
00:00:57,767 --> 00:01:02,041
You are inferior
and will be reborn as Cybermen.

15
00:01:02,081 --> 00:01:06,055
But you will perish
under maximum deletion.

16
00:01:06,953 --> 00:01:10,512
Delete, delete, delete.

17
00:01:52,241 --> 00:01:53,521
What the hell was that? !

18
00:01:53,561 --> 00:01:55,278
Or, how about instead, run!

19
00:01:55,318 --> 00:01:57,325
CAR HORN BEEPS

20
00:02:00,192 --> 00:02:01,705
Everybody! In!

21
00:02:03,904 --> 00:02:06,020
I've got to go back.
My wife's in there.

22
00:02:06,060 --> 00:02:08,136
Anyone inside that house is dead.

23
00:02:08,176 --> 00:02:11,729
Don't let her die for nothing,
come with us right now.

24
00:02:11,769 --> 00:02:14,528
Come on! Get a move on!

25
00:02:14,568 --> 00:02:16,243
Rose. She's not your mother.

26
00:02:16,283 --> 00:02:17,766
I know. Come on.

27
00:02:19,241 --> 00:02:23,005
Finished chatting? Never seen
a slower getaway in my life!

28
00:02:40,208 --> 00:02:42,124
What was that thing?

29
00:02:42,164 --> 00:02:44,443
Little bit of technology
from my home.

30
00:02:44,483 --> 00:02:49,151
Has it run out? It'll charge
back up in about four hours.

31
00:02:49,191 --> 00:02:50,867
So we don't have a weapon. We do.

32
00:02:50,907 --> 00:02:55,181
Might not work on those metal
things, but they're good enough
for men like him.

33
00:02:55,221 --> 00:02:57,178
Leave him alone!
What's he done wrong?

34
00:02:57,218 --> 00:03:01,012
Laid a trap that's wiped out the
government and left Lumic in charge!

35
00:03:01,052 --> 00:03:03,849
If I was part of that, do you think
I'd leave my wife inside?

36
00:03:03,889 --> 00:03:07,004
Maybe it went wrong. Still gives us
the right to execute you.

37
00:03:07,044 --> 00:03:11,079
Talk about executions,
you'll make me your enemy.
You don't want to do that.

38
00:03:11,119 --> 00:03:16,969
All the same, we have evidence
that says Pete Tyler's been
working for the Lumics since 20.5.

39
00:03:19,825 --> 00:03:20,814
Is that true?

40
00:03:22,544 --> 00:03:24,134
Tell 'em, Mrs M.

41
00:03:24,174 --> 00:03:27,094
We've got a government mole,
feeds us information.

42
00:03:27,134 --> 00:03:30,845
Lumic's private files, his
South American operations, the lot.

43
00:03:30,885 --> 00:03:33,082
Secret broadcasts twice a week.

44
00:03:33,122 --> 00:03:35,880
Broadcasts from Gemini?
And how do you know that?

45
00:03:35,920 --> 00:03:38,595
I'm Gemini! That's me!
You would say that.

46
00:03:38,635 --> 00:03:42,271
Encrypted wavelength 657
using binary nine.

47
00:03:42,311 --> 00:03:46,102
That's the only reason I was working
for Lumic. To get information.

48
00:03:46,142 --> 00:03:48,978
I thought it was the
security services, what do I get?

49
00:03:49,018 --> 00:03:51,414
The Scooby Doo gang!
They've even got the van!

50
00:03:51,454 --> 00:03:55,848
No, no, but the Preachers
know what they're doing. Ricky
said he's London's most wanted.

51
00:03:55,888 --> 00:03:57,764
Yeah, that's not exactly. . .

52
00:03:57,804 --> 00:03:59,283
Not exactly what?

53
00:03:59,323 --> 00:04:02,682
I'm London's most wanted
for parking tickets.

54
00:04:03,793 --> 00:04:05,589
Oh, great.

55
00:04:05,629 --> 00:04:08,069
I was fighting the system!
Park anywhere.

56
00:04:08,108 --> 00:04:09,904
Good policy. I do much the same.

57
00:04:09,944 --> 00:04:12,619
I'm the Doctor, by the way,
if anyone's interested.

58
00:04:12,659 --> 00:04:15,974
And I'm Rose. Hello! Even better.
That's the name of my dog.

59
00:04:16,014 --> 00:04:19,769
Still, at least I've got
the catering staff on my side.

60
00:04:19,809 --> 00:04:21,606
I knew you weren't a traitor.

61
00:04:21,646 --> 00:04:23,209
Why's that then?

62
00:04:24,881 --> 00:04:27,098
I just did.

63
00:04:28,597 --> 00:04:30,156
They took my wife.

64
00:04:30,196 --> 00:04:31,671
She might still be alive.

65
00:04:31,711 --> 00:04:33,350
That's even worse.

66
00:04:33,390 --> 00:04:35,028
Cos that's what Lumic does.

67
00:04:35,068 --> 00:04:37,499
He takes the living. . .

68
00:04:37,539 --> 00:04:40,177
and turns them into those machines.

69
00:04:40,217 --> 00:04:46,246
Cybermen. They're called Cybermen.
And I'd take those Ear Pods
off if I were you.

70
00:04:46,286 --> 00:04:49,402
You never know,
Lumic could be listening.

71
00:04:49,442 --> 00:04:53,938
But he's over reached himself,
he's a businessman
who's assassinated the President.

72
00:04:53,978 --> 00:04:56,172
All we need to do
is inform the authorities.

73
00:04:56,212 --> 00:04:59,037
Because I promise you,
this ends tonight.

74
00:05:00,129 --> 00:05:06,716
My everlasting children. Tell me,
how does it feel? We feel nothing.

75
00:05:06,756 --> 00:05:09,152
But in your mind.
What do you think?

76
00:05:09,192 --> 00:05:11,311
We think the same.

77
00:05:11,351 --> 00:05:15,580
We are uniform.
But you think of what?

78
00:05:15,620 --> 00:05:19,972
We think of the humans. We think
of their difference and their pain.

79
00:05:20,012 --> 00:05:22,130
They suffer in the skin.

80
00:05:22,170 --> 00:05:24,006
They must be upgraded.

81
00:05:24,046 --> 00:05:27,922
Excellent, then let's begin.

82
00:05:27,962 --> 00:05:30,437
Computer, identify John Lumic.

83
00:05:30,477 --> 00:05:32,635
'Voice print acknowledged.'

84
00:05:32,675 --> 00:05:34,912
Activate Ear Pod Primary Sequence.

85
00:05:34,952 --> 00:05:37,748
'Please state area of activation.'

86
00:05:37,788 --> 00:05:43,179
The City of London.
I've just declared independence.

87
00:05:43,218 --> 00:05:44,987
Begin transmission!

88
00:05:50,490 --> 00:05:52,616
ALARM BEEPS

89
00:06:05,943 --> 00:06:07,978
They will come to me.

90
00:06:08,018 --> 00:06:09,656
My new children.

91
00:06:09,696 --> 00:06:11,892
The immortal ones.

92
00:06:11,932 --> 00:06:14,008
The whole of London
has been sealed off.

93
00:06:14,048 --> 00:06:15,687
There are reports of an army.

94
00:06:15,727 --> 00:06:18,962
An army of metal men. All citizens
should remove their Ear Pods.

95
00:06:19,002 --> 00:06:23,156
I repeat, remove all Ear Pods.
London has been placed
under martial law.

96
00:06:23,196 --> 00:06:27,045
If you are hearing this, stay in your
homes. I repeat, stay in your homes.

97
00:06:28,305 --> 00:06:30,781
ELECTRICAL BUZZING, MAN GROANS

98
00:06:30,821 --> 00:06:33,896
Oh, no, you don't!

99
00:06:33,936 --> 00:06:37,333
What the hell? What's going on?

100
00:06:37,373 --> 00:06:41,086
It's the Ear Pods, Lumic's
taken control. Can't we just. . .

101
00:06:41,126 --> 00:06:43,404
I dunno, take them off? Don't!

102
00:06:43,444 --> 00:06:45,240
Cause a brainstorm.

103
00:06:45,280 --> 00:06:49,314
The human race
for such an intelligent lot,
you aren't half susceptible.

104
00:06:49,354 --> 00:06:52,030
Give anyone a chance to
take control and you submit!

105
00:06:52,070 --> 00:06:54,586
Sometimes I think you like it
an easy life.

106
00:06:54,626 --> 00:06:56,837
Hey! Come and see!

107
00:07:02,216 --> 00:07:04,529
Where are they all going?

108
00:07:04,569 --> 00:07:07,164
I don't know. Lumic must
have a base of operations.

109
00:07:07,204 --> 00:07:11,397
Battersea. That's where
he was building his prototypes.

110
00:07:11,437 --> 00:07:14,432
Why's he doing it? He's dying.

111
00:07:14,471 --> 00:07:18,268
This all started out
as a way of prolonging life,
keeping the brain alive.

112
00:07:18,308 --> 00:07:21,663
At any cost. Thing is, I've seen
Cybermen before, haven't I?

113
00:07:21,703 --> 00:07:24,858
The head, those handle shapes.
In Van Statten's Museum.

114
00:07:24,898 --> 00:07:30,569
There are Cybermen in our universe.
They started on an ordinary world,
then swarmed across the galaxy.

115
00:07:30,609 --> 00:07:33,604
This lot are starting from scratch,
right here on Earth.

116
00:07:33,644 --> 00:07:34,883
What are you on about?

117
00:07:34,923 --> 00:07:37,759
Never mind that,
we need to get out of the city.

118
00:07:37,799 --> 00:07:40,675
OK, split up! Mrs Moore,
you look after that lot.

119
00:07:40,715 --> 00:07:43,619
Jake, distract them. We'll
meet back at Bridge Street. Move!

120
00:07:44,427 --> 00:07:45,870
I'm going with him.

121
00:07:47,420 --> 00:07:49,182
Come on! Let's go.

122
00:07:53,370 --> 00:07:54,928
There!

123
00:08:08,428 --> 00:08:10,385
Which way?
I don't know where we are.

124
00:08:10,425 --> 00:08:14,259
Did they see us? Bet they've got
satellites. They saw us in the dark.

125
00:08:14,299 --> 00:08:16,017
BOTH: They know where we are.

126
00:08:16,057 --> 00:08:17,856
I don't get it, what is it with you?

127
00:08:17,896 --> 00:08:19,648
You're exactly like me.

128
00:08:19,688 --> 00:08:22,366
I dunno. Reckon you're braver.
Ten times.

129
00:08:22,405 --> 00:08:24,762
Still, your friends aren't bad.

130
00:08:24,802 --> 00:08:27,957
That's the Doctor and Rose.
I just tag along behind.

131
00:08:27,997 --> 00:08:29,876
Well, then you're not that bad.

132
00:08:29,916 --> 00:08:32,389
Do you think? Yeah, suppose.

133
00:08:32,429 --> 00:08:34,276
METALLIC MARCHING

134
00:08:35,745 --> 00:08:36,779
Cybermen!

135
00:08:38,139 --> 00:08:39,128
BOTH: Split up!

136
00:09:14,324 --> 00:09:15,881
(Go!)

137
00:09:23,590 --> 00:09:28,980
TANNOY: 'Chamber 12 now closed
for sterilisation.

138
00:09:29,020 --> 00:09:33,529
'All reject stock
will be in incinerated.'

139
00:09:51,306 --> 00:09:53,262
Come on!

140
00:09:53,302 --> 00:09:55,179
Come on!

141
00:09:55,219 --> 00:09:56,738
Come on!

142
00:09:56,778 --> 00:09:57,857
HE SCREAMS

143
00:09:57,897 --> 00:09:59,210
No!

144
00:10:15,827 --> 00:10:18,342
Cyberman: This one is unprogrammed.

145
00:10:18,382 --> 00:10:21,538
Mr Crane, I thought you
were one of the faithful.

146
00:10:21,578 --> 00:10:23,013
Oh, that I am, sir.

147
00:10:23,053 --> 00:10:25,210
My Ear Pod must have malfunctioned.

148
00:10:25,250 --> 00:10:27,168
For which I apologise.

149
00:10:27,208 --> 00:10:28,691
If I might?

150
00:10:32,320 --> 00:10:34,397
I'd like to request an upgrade, sir.

151
00:10:34,436 --> 00:10:38,192
I've seen the future
and its copyright Cybus Industries.

152
00:10:38,232 --> 00:10:41,308
Sign me up! A willing volunteer?

153
00:10:41,348 --> 00:10:43,303
You've known me a long time, sir.

154
00:10:43,343 --> 00:10:44,940
Quite a team, you and me.

155
00:10:44,980 --> 00:10:47,215
I've been with you all the way.

156
00:10:47,255 --> 00:10:48,932
But believe me, sir.

157
00:10:48,972 --> 00:10:53,071
Knowing you so well,
I know exactly what to do.

158
00:10:57,402 --> 00:10:59,210
No! No! Help me!

159
00:11:02,393 --> 00:11:03,337
Die!

160
00:11:05,388 --> 00:11:07,664
Help me! You are in pain.

161
00:11:07,704 --> 00:11:10,103
We can remove pain forever.

162
00:11:10,143 --> 00:11:13,578
No. Not yet. I'm not ready!

163
00:11:13,618 --> 00:11:15,934
We will give you immortality.

164
00:11:15,974 --> 00:11:19,130
I've told you, I will upgrade. . .

165
00:11:19,170 --> 00:11:20,888
only with my last breath.

166
00:11:20,928 --> 00:11:24,401
Then breathe no more.

167
00:11:26,114 --> 00:11:30,048
No, no! I command you! No!

168
00:11:33,224 --> 00:11:37,177
I ran past the river,
you should've seen it
the whole city's on the march.

169
00:11:37,217 --> 00:11:39,224
Hundreds of Cybermen
all down the Thames.

170
00:11:40,335 --> 00:11:41,858
Here he is!

171
00:11:43,928 --> 00:11:45,804
Which one are you?

172
00:11:45,844 --> 00:11:48,965
I'm sorry. The Cybermen. . .
He couldn't. . . Are you Ricky?

173
00:11:49,881 --> 00:11:51,200
Are you Ricky?

174
00:11:51,240 --> 00:11:52,953
Mickey, that's you, isn't it?

175
00:11:52,993 --> 00:11:54,761
Yeah.

176
00:11:59,665 --> 00:12:01,417
He tried. He was running.

177
00:12:01,457 --> 00:12:03,697
There was too many of them. Shut it.

178
00:12:03,736 --> 00:12:07,129
There was nothing I could do.
I said just shut it!

179
00:12:07,169 --> 00:12:09,289
Don't even talk about him.

180
00:12:09,329 --> 00:12:11,619
You're nothing, you are.

181
00:12:13,439 --> 00:12:14,997
Nothing.

182
00:12:16,078 --> 00:12:19,313
We can mourn him
when London is safe.

183
00:12:19,353 --> 00:12:21,439
For now, we move on.

184
00:12:43,312 --> 00:12:48,545
The whole of London's been sealed
off and the entire population's
been taken inside that place.

185
00:12:48,585 --> 00:12:50,981
To be converted.

186
00:12:51,021 --> 00:12:53,138
We've got to get in there
and shut it down.

187
00:12:53,178 --> 00:12:54,815
How do we do that?

188
00:12:54,855 --> 00:12:56,654
Oh, I'll think of something.

189
00:12:56,694 --> 00:13:00,009
You're just making this up
as you go along! Yep.

190
00:13:00,048 --> 00:13:01,691
But I do it brilliantly.

191
00:13:03,604 --> 00:13:07,083
MRS MOORE: That's a schematic
of the old factory.

192
00:13:08,555 --> 00:13:11,471
Look, cooling tunnels
underneath the plant,

193
00:13:11,511 --> 00:13:15,982
big enough to walk through.
We go under,
then up into the control centre.

194
00:13:16,022 --> 00:13:18,778
There's another way in.
Through the front door.

195
00:13:18,818 --> 00:13:21,774
If they've taken Jackie,
that's how she'll get in.

196
00:13:21,814 --> 00:13:24,050
We can't just go strolling up.

197
00:13:24,090 --> 00:13:27,604
Oh, we could. With these.

198
00:13:27,644 --> 00:13:29,839
Fake Ear Pods.

199
00:13:29,879 --> 00:13:34,633
Dead, no signal, but put them on
and the Cybermen would mistake you
for one of the crowd.

200
00:13:34,673 --> 00:13:36,231
Then that's my job.

201
00:13:36,271 --> 00:13:39,744
You'd have to show no emotion.
Any sign of emotion gives you away.

202
00:13:39,784 --> 00:13:42,023
How many of those have you got?
Just two sets.

203
00:13:42,063 --> 00:13:43,858
OK.

204
00:13:43,898 --> 00:13:48,374
If that's the best way of finding
Jackie, then I'm coming with you.

205
00:13:48,414 --> 00:13:53,042
Why does she matter to you?
We haven't got time.
Doctor, I'm going with him.

206
00:13:53,082 --> 00:13:54,641
No stopping you, is there?

207
00:13:54,681 --> 00:13:56,836
Nope.

208
00:13:56,876 --> 00:14:00,114
Tell you what, we can attack
the Ear Pods at the same time.

209
00:14:00,154 --> 00:14:06,413
Give people their minds back,
so they don't walk into that place
like sheep. Jakey boy. . .

210
00:14:09,459 --> 00:14:13,348
Lumic's transmitting the control
signal. It must be from over there.

211
00:14:15,250 --> 00:14:18,165
There it is.
On the zeppelin, do you see?

212
00:14:18,205 --> 00:14:22,238
Great big transmitter. It's a good
thing Lumic likes showing off.

213
00:14:22,278 --> 00:14:24,037
Reckon you can take it out?

214
00:14:24,077 --> 00:14:26,712
Consider it done.

215
00:14:26,752 --> 00:14:30,662
Mrs Moore,
would you care to accompany me
into the cooling tunnels?

216
00:14:30,702 --> 00:14:33,900
How could I refuse?
We attack on three sides.

217
00:14:33,940 --> 00:14:39,650
Above, between, below. Into the
control centre, stop the conversion
machines. What about me?

218
00:14:39,690 --> 00:14:43,443
Mickey, you can, um. . .

219
00:14:43,483 --> 00:14:46,402
What? Stay out of trouble?
Be the tin dog?

220
00:14:46,442 --> 00:14:47,998
No, those days are over.

221
00:14:48,038 --> 00:14:50,474
I'm going with Jake.
I don't need you, idiot.

222
00:14:50,514 --> 00:14:53,189
I'm not an idiot. You got that?

223
00:14:53,229 --> 00:14:54,746
I'm offering to help.

224
00:14:56,743 --> 00:14:58,551
Whatever.

225
00:15:01,059 --> 00:15:02,935
Mickey!

226
00:15:02,975 --> 00:15:04,255
Good luck.

227
00:15:04,294 --> 00:15:06,128
Yeah, you too.

228
00:15:06,168 --> 00:15:09,203
Rose, I'll see you later.
Yeah! You'd better.

229
00:15:09,243 --> 00:15:11,579
If we survive,
I'll see you at the Tardis.

230
00:15:15,835 --> 00:15:17,768
That's a promise.

231
00:15:23,064 --> 00:15:25,065
Good luck.

232
00:15:40,398 --> 00:15:43,149
It's freezing.

233
00:15:43,189 --> 00:15:45,867
Any sign of a light switch?

234
00:15:45,907 --> 00:15:49,142
Can't see a thing.
But I've got these.

235
00:15:49,182 --> 00:15:50,977
A device for every occasion. Ooh!

236
00:15:51,017 --> 00:15:52,330
Put it on.

237
00:15:54,373 --> 00:15:57,730
Haven't got a hot dog in there,
have you? I'm starving.

238
00:15:57,770 --> 00:16:01,599
Of all the things to wish for,
that's mechanically recovered meat.

239
00:16:01,639 --> 00:16:05,796
I know, it's the Cyberman of food.
But it's tasty!

240
00:16:05,836 --> 00:16:07,910
A proper torch as well.

241
00:16:07,950 --> 00:16:09,467
Let's see where we are.

242
00:16:13,862 --> 00:16:18,034
Already converted, just put on ice.
Come on.

243
00:16:28,240 --> 00:16:29,957
Let's go slowly.

244
00:16:33,511 --> 00:16:36,171
Keep an eye out for trip systems.

245
00:16:56,636 --> 00:16:59,706
TANNOY MAKES AN ANNOUNCEMENT

246
00:17:12,846 --> 00:17:16,206
Just put them on.
Don't show any emotion.

247
00:17:16,246 --> 00:17:18,240
No signs, nothing. OK?

248
00:17:18,280 --> 00:17:20,876
Don't worry. We can do it.

249
00:17:20,916 --> 00:17:23,713
We could die in there.
Why you doing this?

250
00:17:23,753 --> 00:17:26,453
Let's just say I'm doing it
for my mum and dad.

251
00:17:27,227 --> 00:17:29,478
Right, let's go.

252
00:17:30,939 --> 00:17:34,931
TANNOY: 'Chamber eight now
open for human upgrading.

253
00:17:34,971 --> 00:17:40,842
'Chamber nine now open
for human upgrading.

254
00:17:40,882 --> 00:17:46,163
'Chamber ten now open
for human upgrading.

255
00:17:50,228 --> 00:17:55,913
'Chamber 11 now open
for human upgrading.'

256
00:18:28,128 --> 00:18:30,967
Two guards. We can take them.

257
00:18:31,007 --> 00:18:33,043
Don't kill them.
Who put you in charge?

258
00:18:33,083 --> 00:18:36,852
If you kill them,
what's the difference between you
and a Cyberman?

259
00:18:38,474 --> 00:18:40,850
Well, I suppose we could use these.

260
00:18:42,469 --> 00:18:43,944
Smelling salts?

261
00:18:43,984 --> 00:18:47,540
Bit stronger than that.
One of Mrs Moore's little tricks.

262
00:18:47,580 --> 00:18:49,533
Should knock 'em out.

263
00:18:49,573 --> 00:18:52,114
(Three, two, one.)

264
00:19:05,430 --> 00:19:07,647
There's got to be more guards
on board.

265
00:19:08,347 --> 00:19:09,984
Then let's go get them.

266
00:19:15,176 --> 00:19:17,213
How did you get into this, then?

267
00:19:17,253 --> 00:19:19,689
Rattling along with the Preachers.

268
00:19:19,729 --> 00:19:22,964
Oh, I used to be ordinary!

269
00:19:23,004 --> 00:19:26,636
Worked at Cybus Industries,
nine to five.

270
00:19:26,676 --> 00:19:30,868
Till one day I find something
I'm not supposed to.

271
00:19:30,908 --> 00:19:33,346
A file on the mainframe.

272
00:19:33,386 --> 00:19:35,782
All I did was read it.

273
00:19:35,822 --> 00:19:40,694
Then suddenly I've got men with guns
knocking in the middle of the night.

274
00:19:40,734 --> 00:19:42,730
A life on the run.

275
00:19:42,770 --> 00:19:45,649
Then I found the Preachers.

276
00:19:45,689 --> 00:19:48,325
They needed a techie, so I. . .

277
00:19:48,365 --> 00:19:50,880
just sat down
and taught myself everything.

278
00:19:50,920 --> 00:19:52,835
What about Mr Moore?

279
00:19:52,875 --> 00:19:54,847
Well, he's not called Moore.

280
00:19:56,391 --> 00:19:58,107
I got that from a book,

281
00:19:58,147 --> 00:20:00,546
Mrs Moore.

282
00:20:00,586 --> 00:20:02,843
It's safer not to use real names.

283
00:20:04,338 --> 00:20:08,770
But he thinks I'm dead.
It was the only way to keep him safe.

284
00:20:08,810 --> 00:20:10,578
Him and the kids.

285
00:20:12,485 --> 00:20:14,201
What about you,

286
00:20:14,241 --> 00:20:15,718
got any family?

287
00:20:15,758 --> 00:20:17,917
Who needs family?

288
00:20:17,957 --> 00:20:20,553
I've got the whole world
on my shoulders.

289
00:20:20,593 --> 00:20:24,587
Go on then, what's your real name?

290
00:20:24,627 --> 00:20:27,463
Angela Price.

291
00:20:27,503 --> 00:20:29,058
Don't tell a soul.

292
00:20:29,098 --> 00:20:31,070
Not a word.

293
00:20:42,198 --> 00:20:44,939
Movement in Deepcold Six.

294
00:20:45,753 --> 00:20:47,924
Awaken the army.

295
00:20:50,144 --> 00:20:53,500
Doctor? Did that one move?

296
00:20:53,540 --> 00:20:55,775
It's just the torchlight.

297
00:20:55,815 --> 00:20:57,335
Keep going, come on.

298
00:20:57,375 --> 00:20:59,507
They're waking up! Run!

299
00:21:11,873 --> 00:21:14,828
Get up! Quick, they're coming!

300
00:21:14,868 --> 00:21:18,301
Open it! Open it!

301
00:21:18,341 --> 00:21:20,895
Get up, quick!

302
00:21:20,935 --> 00:21:23,271
Quick! Angela! Come on!

303
00:21:31,162 --> 00:21:33,664
Oh, good team, Mrs Moore!

304
00:21:36,154 --> 00:21:41,305
TANNOY: 'Units upgraded. Now 6,500.

305
00:21:41,345 --> 00:21:46,137
'Repeat, 6,500 and rising.'

306
00:21:52,290 --> 00:21:53,882
You will wait.

307
00:21:55,243 --> 00:21:56,755
You OK?

308
00:21:57,919 --> 00:21:59,239
No.

309
00:21:59,279 --> 00:22:02,718
TANNOY: 'Chamber six
now open for human upgrading.

310
00:22:05,785 --> 00:22:09,060
'All reject stock will be
incinerated.'

311
00:22:44,644 --> 00:22:46,088
Any sign of Jackie?

312
00:22:49,279 --> 00:22:52,035
You are Peter Tyler.

313
00:22:52,075 --> 00:22:54,631
Confirm. You are Peter Tyler.

314
00:22:54,671 --> 00:22:56,426
Confirm.

315
00:22:56,466 --> 00:23:01,418
I recognise you. I went first
my name was Jacqueline Tyler.

316
00:23:01,458 --> 00:23:05,651
No! What?
They are unprogrammed. Restrain.

317
00:23:05,691 --> 00:23:09,045
You're lying, you're not her,
you're not my Jackie.

318
00:23:09,085 --> 00:23:10,641
No, I am Cyberform.

319
00:23:10,681 --> 00:23:13,118
Once I was Jacqueline Tyler.

320
00:23:13,158 --> 00:23:14,960
But you can't be.

321
00:23:15,755 --> 00:23:19,192
Not her. . .
Her brain is inside this body.

322
00:23:19,232 --> 00:23:21,386
Jacks. I came to save you!

323
00:23:21,426 --> 00:23:26,059
This man worked with Cybus
Industries to create our species.

324
00:23:26,099 --> 00:23:28,015
He will be rewarded by force.

325
00:23:28,055 --> 00:23:31,301
Take them to Cybercontrol.

326
00:23:33,529 --> 00:23:35,685
They killed her.

327
00:23:35,725 --> 00:23:37,801
They took her and killed her.
Maybe there's a chance.

328
00:23:37,841 --> 00:23:41,316
I don't know, maybe we can reverse
it. There's nothing we can do.

329
00:23:41,356 --> 00:23:43,363
But if she remembers. . .

330
00:23:45,588 --> 00:23:48,420
Where is she?
Which one was it? Which one was her?

331
00:23:50,699 --> 00:23:52,916
They all look the same.

332
00:23:56,651 --> 00:23:59,206
Nice one, nobody's home.

333
00:23:59,246 --> 00:24:01,123
Find the controls.
What do they look like?

334
00:24:01,163 --> 00:24:05,012
They might have transmitter controls
written in red letters, just look!

335
00:24:11,948 --> 00:24:14,324
Whoa! Cyberman!

336
00:24:31,594 --> 00:24:34,550
It's dead.

337
00:24:34,590 --> 00:24:36,437
I don't think it was ever alive.

338
00:24:40,941 --> 00:24:45,729
It's empty. No brain, just
the robot suit. It's for display.

339
00:24:48,092 --> 00:24:49,285
Transmitter!

340
00:24:58,112 --> 00:25:00,349
You are not upgraded.

341
00:25:00,389 --> 00:25:03,181
Yeah, well, upgrade this.

342
00:25:10,493 --> 00:25:14,208
What the hell was that thing?
Electromagnetic bomb.

343
00:25:14,248 --> 00:25:18,163
It takes out computers,
I figured it might stop a cybersuit.

344
00:25:18,203 --> 00:25:20,718
Well, you figured right.
Now let's have a look.

345
00:25:20,758 --> 00:25:24,671
Know your enemy. They've even
got the logo on the front.

346
00:25:24,711 --> 00:25:27,536
Lumic's turned them into a brand.

347
00:25:29,507 --> 00:25:31,713
Heart of steel.

348
00:25:34,697 --> 00:25:35,890
But look. . .

349
00:25:38,489 --> 00:25:41,404
Is that flesh? Mmm.

350
00:25:41,444 --> 00:25:43,243
A central nervous system.

351
00:25:43,283 --> 00:25:46,756
Artificially grown, threaded
through the suit so it responds
like a living thing.

352
00:25:46,796 --> 00:25:50,232
Well, it is a living thing.

353
00:25:50,272 --> 00:25:51,835
Oh, but look!

354
00:25:52,867 --> 00:25:55,102
Emotional inhibitor.

355
00:25:55,142 --> 00:25:56,942
Stops them feeling anything.

356
00:25:56,982 --> 00:25:58,938
But why?

357
00:25:58,978 --> 00:26:00,455
It's still got a human brain.

358
00:26:00,495 --> 00:26:02,175
Imagine its reaction

359
00:26:02,215 --> 00:26:06,210
if it could see itself,
realise itself, inside this thing.

360
00:26:06,250 --> 00:26:08,924
It would go insane.

361
00:26:08,964 --> 00:26:11,999
So they cut out the one
thing that makes them human.

362
00:26:12,039 --> 00:26:14,352
Because they have to.

363
00:26:14,392 --> 00:26:17,428
Why. . .am I. . .cold?

364
00:26:17,468 --> 00:26:19,663
Oh, my God, it's alive.

365
00:26:19,703 --> 00:26:21,661
It can feel. We broke the inhibitor.

366
00:26:21,701 --> 00:26:24,218
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

367
00:26:24,258 --> 00:26:26,454
Why so cold?

368
00:26:26,494 --> 00:26:28,093
Can you remember your name?

369
00:26:28,133 --> 00:26:31,527
Sally. Sally Phelan.

370
00:26:31,765 --> 00:26:33,165
You're a woman.

371
00:26:33,205 --> 00:26:35,480
Where's Gareth?

372
00:26:35,520 --> 00:26:37,120
Who's Gareth?

373
00:26:37,160 --> 00:26:39,516
He can't see me.

374
00:26:39,556 --> 00:26:43,190
It's unlucky the night before.

375
00:26:43,230 --> 00:26:45,467
You're getting married?

376
00:26:45,507 --> 00:26:47,379
I'm cold.

377
00:26:47,419 --> 00:26:50,655
I'm so cold.

378
00:26:50,695 --> 00:26:54,449
It's all right.
You sleep now, Sally.

379
00:26:54,489 --> 00:26:57,234
Just go to sleep.

380
00:27:00,638 --> 00:27:03,717
Sally Phelan didn't die for nothing.

381
00:27:03,757 --> 00:27:06,353
Because that's the key,

382
00:27:06,393 --> 00:27:08,149
the emotional inhibitor.

383
00:27:08,189 --> 00:27:11,584
If we can find the cancellation
code, feed it throughout the system

384
00:27:11,624 --> 00:27:14,659
into every Cyberman's head,
they'd realise what they are.

385
00:27:14,699 --> 00:27:17,055
And what happens then?

386
00:27:17,095 --> 00:27:18,567
I think it would kill them.

387
00:27:20,531 --> 00:27:22,050
Can we do that?

388
00:27:22,090 --> 00:27:25,530
We've got to.
Before they kill everyone else.

389
00:27:26,800 --> 00:27:29,154
There's no choice, Doctor.

390
00:27:29,194 --> 00:27:31,496
It's got to be done.

391
00:27:38,621 --> 00:27:41,257
No! No, you didn't have to kill her!

392
00:27:41,297 --> 00:27:44,372
Sensors detect
a binary vascular system.

393
00:27:44,412 --> 00:27:46,688
You are an unknown upgrade.

394
00:27:46,728 --> 00:27:50,008
You will be taken for analysis.

395
00:27:58,035 --> 00:28:01,860
The transmitter controls are sealed
behind here, we need oxy acetylene.

396
00:28:01,900 --> 00:28:04,737
Oh, and I forgot to bring it with me.
Then what do we do?

397
00:28:04,777 --> 00:28:05,977
We crash the zeppelin.

398
00:28:06,017 --> 00:28:09,412
With us inside it? We could set it
on automatic and then just leg it.

399
00:28:09,452 --> 00:28:11,060
Let's have a look.

400
00:28:16,362 --> 00:28:18,955
It's locked.
There's gotta be an override.

401
00:28:18,995 --> 00:28:21,832
Let me have a go.
I'm good with computers, trust me.

402
00:28:41,959 --> 00:28:45,872
I've been captured, but don't worry,
Rose and Pete are still out there,

403
00:28:45,912 --> 00:28:48,031
they can rescue me.
Never mind. You OK?

404
00:28:48,071 --> 00:28:49,867
Yeah.

405
00:28:49,907 --> 00:28:51,543
But they got Jackie.

406
00:28:51,583 --> 00:28:53,822
We were too late. Lumic killed her.

407
00:28:53,862 --> 00:28:55,417
Then where is he?

408
00:28:55,457 --> 00:28:57,455
The famous Mr Lumic.

409
00:28:57,495 --> 00:29:00,293
Don't we get the chance
to meet our lord and master?

410
00:29:00,333 --> 00:29:02,927
He has been upgraded.

411
00:29:02,967 --> 00:29:06,124
So he's just like you.
He is superior.

412
00:29:06,164 --> 00:29:10,582
The Lumic unit has been designated
Cybercontroller.

413
00:29:19,143 --> 00:29:21,418
This is the Age of Steel.

414
00:29:21,458 --> 00:29:23,999
And I am its creator.

415
00:29:29,446 --> 00:29:31,245
I'm almost there.

416
00:29:31,285 --> 00:29:33,292
Not bad work.

417
00:29:38,192 --> 00:29:39,954
It's moving!

418
00:29:41,668 --> 00:29:43,187
You said it was dead!

419
00:29:43,227 --> 00:29:45,103
A robot suit's still a good robot!
Wait!

420
00:29:45,143 --> 00:29:46,865
Hey, Cyberman! Over here!

421
00:29:49,255 --> 00:29:52,120
Come on, you brainless lump
of metal! Come and have a go!

422
00:30:04,269 --> 00:30:05,548
Oh, no!

423
00:30:05,588 --> 00:30:07,640
THEY SCREAM

424
00:30:08,463 --> 00:30:09,986
The transmitter's down!

425
00:30:18,448 --> 00:30:20,886
MUFFLED SCREAMS

426
00:30:20,926 --> 00:30:23,722
That's my friends at work.
Good boys!

427
00:30:23,762 --> 00:30:27,314
Mr Lumic, I think that's
a vote for free will!

428
00:30:27,354 --> 00:30:31,945
I have factories waiting
on seven continents.

429
00:30:31,985 --> 00:30:38,415
If the Ear Pods have failed, then the
Cybermen will take humanity by force.

430
00:30:38,455 --> 00:30:41,611
London has fallen.

431
00:30:41,651 --> 00:30:43,966
So shall the world.

432
00:30:44,006 --> 00:30:48,842
Hold on, I've logged on to
Cybercontrol. They're alive!
The Doctor and Rose, there they are!

433
00:30:48,882 --> 00:30:50,478
What the hell is that thing?

434
00:30:50,518 --> 00:30:53,154
Shh! Has this thing got sound?

435
00:30:53,194 --> 00:30:56,830
'I will bring peace to the world.

436
00:30:56,870 --> 00:30:58,585
'Everlasting peace. . .'

437
00:30:58,625 --> 00:31:02,420
and unity and uniformity.

438
00:31:02,460 --> 00:31:04,256
And imagination? What about that?

439
00:31:04,296 --> 00:31:08,289
The one thing that led you here,
imagination, you're killing it dead.

440
00:31:08,329 --> 00:31:10,364
What is your name?

441
00:31:10,404 --> 00:31:12,921
I'm the Doctor. A redundant title.

442
00:31:12,961 --> 00:31:14,879
Doctors need not exist.

443
00:31:14,919 --> 00:31:16,755
Cybermen never sicken.

444
00:31:16,795 --> 00:31:20,151
Yeah, but that's it,
that's exactly the point.

445
00:31:20,191 --> 00:31:22,027
Oh, Lumic, you're a clever man.

446
00:31:22,067 --> 00:31:25,941
I'd call you a genius, except I'm
here. Everything you've invented,

447
00:31:25,981 --> 00:31:28,338
you did to fight your sickness
brilliant.

448
00:31:28,378 --> 00:31:30,057
That is so human.

449
00:31:30,097 --> 00:31:35,889
But once you get rid of
sickness and mortality, then
what's there to strive for? Eh?

450
00:31:35,929 --> 00:31:37,884
The Cybermen won't advance.

451
00:31:37,924 --> 00:31:39,440
You'll just stop.

452
00:31:39,480 --> 00:31:41,599
You'll stay like this for ever.

453
00:31:41,639 --> 00:31:45,588
A metal Earth
with metal men and metal thoughts.

454
00:31:45,628 --> 00:31:49,742
Lacking the one thing that makes
this planet so alive. People!

455
00:31:49,782 --> 00:31:53,539
Ordinary, stupid, brilliant, people!

456
00:31:53,579 --> 00:31:56,453
You are proud of your emotions?

457
00:31:56,493 --> 00:31:57,613
Oh, yes!

458
00:31:57,652 --> 00:31:59,529
Then tell me, Doctor,

459
00:31:59,569 --> 00:32:01,204
have you known grief?

460
00:32:01,244 --> 00:32:03,521
And rage? And pain?

461
00:32:03,561 --> 00:32:05,599
Yes. Yes, I have.

462
00:32:05,639 --> 00:32:07,355
And they hurt?

463
00:32:07,395 --> 00:32:09,155
Oh, yes.

464
00:32:09,195 --> 00:32:11,349
I can set you free.

465
00:32:11,389 --> 00:32:13,149
Would you not want that?

466
00:32:13,188 --> 00:32:15,066
A life without pain.

467
00:32:15,106 --> 00:32:17,100
You might as well kill me.

468
00:32:17,140 --> 00:32:19,938
Then I take that option.

469
00:32:19,978 --> 00:32:21,770
It's not yours to take!

470
00:32:21,810 --> 00:32:23,409
You're a Cybercontroller.

471
00:32:23,449 --> 00:32:26,126
You don't control me,
or anything with a heart.

472
00:32:26,166 --> 00:32:28,760
You have no means of stopping me.

473
00:32:28,800 --> 00:32:33,116
I have an army. A species of my own.

474
00:32:33,156 --> 00:32:35,432
You just don't get it, do you?

475
00:32:35,472 --> 00:32:37,148
An army's nothing.

476
00:32:37,188 --> 00:32:42,143
Cos those ordinary people,
they're the key. The most ordinary
person can change the world.

477
00:32:42,183 --> 00:32:43,942
Some ordinary man or woman,

478
00:32:43,982 --> 00:32:48,774
some idiot. All it takes is for him
to find, say, the right numbers. . .

479
00:32:48,814 --> 00:32:53,485
Say, the right code, say,
for example, the code behind
the emotional inhibitor.

480
00:32:53,525 --> 00:32:57,916
The code right in front of him.
Cos even an idiot knows
his computers, these days.

481
00:32:57,956 --> 00:33:02,108
Knows how to get past
firewalls and passwords.

482
00:33:02,148 --> 00:33:07,101
How to find something encrypted in
the Lumic Family database, under
what was it, Pete, binary what?

483
00:33:07,141 --> 00:33:11,136
Binary nine. Binary nine! !
An idiot could find that code!

484
00:33:11,176 --> 00:33:18,206
A cancellation code. He'd keep
on typing, keep on fighting,
anything to save his friends.

485
00:33:18,246 --> 00:33:20,362
Your words are irrelevant.

486
00:33:20,402 --> 00:33:23,077
Yeah, talk too much,
that's my problem.

487
00:33:23,117 --> 00:33:26,032
Lucky I got you that cheap tariff,
Rose. For all our chats.

488
00:33:26,072 --> 00:33:28,589
On your phone. The phone!

489
00:33:28,629 --> 00:33:30,265
You will be deleted.

490
00:33:30,305 --> 00:33:32,623
Yes. Delete. Control. Hash.

491
00:33:32,663 --> 00:33:35,139
Then, of course, my particular
favourite. Send!

492
00:33:35,179 --> 00:33:40,008
Let's not forget how you seduced
all those ordinary people.

493
00:33:40,048 --> 00:33:42,723
MESSAGE ALERT
By making technology
compatible with everything else.

494
00:33:42,763 --> 00:33:43,763
It's for you!

495
00:33:43,803 --> 00:33:45,320
Like this!

496
00:33:55,786 --> 00:33:56,979
Yes!

497
00:34:07,770 --> 00:34:09,408
I'm sorry.

498
00:34:17,670 --> 00:34:21,862
What have you done?
I gave them back their souls.

499
00:34:21,902 --> 00:34:23,981
They can see what you've done,
Lumic.

500
00:34:24,021 --> 00:34:27,453
And it's killing them.
Delete! Delete! Delete!

501
00:34:27,493 --> 00:34:30,569
LUMIC GROANS

502
00:34:44,030 --> 00:34:45,587
There's no way out!

503
00:34:46,386 --> 00:34:50,578
What are you doing?
If that factory blows, this
balloon'll ignite. Take it back!

504
00:34:50,618 --> 00:34:53,034
Mickey, they've had it.
I said, take it back!

505
00:34:56,650 --> 00:34:58,844
We're not leaving them behind.

506
00:34:58,884 --> 00:35:01,346
There's no way
we are leaving them behind.

507
00:35:07,635 --> 00:35:09,113
Hold it!

508
00:35:12,064 --> 00:35:14,228
Rose, can you hear me?
Head for the roof!

509
00:35:14,268 --> 00:35:15,956
He says head for the roof.

510
00:35:30,196 --> 00:35:32,243
HE GROANS

511
00:35:33,632 --> 00:35:36,703
No!

512
00:35:46,090 --> 00:35:50,212
Mickey, where did you learn
to fly that thing? !

513
00:35:50,252 --> 00:35:53,441
Playstation! Just hold on, Rose,
I'm coming to get you.

514
00:36:02,552 --> 00:36:05,099
You can't go any lower! I've got to!

515
00:36:05,139 --> 00:36:07,455
You're gonna crush them!

516
00:36:07,495 --> 00:36:10,171
There's gotta be something,
there's got to be.

517
00:36:10,211 --> 00:36:11,445
Oh, yes!

518
00:36:16,402 --> 00:36:18,983
You've got to be kidding.
Rose, get on!

519
00:36:21,922 --> 00:36:24,412
Hold on tight, we're going up!

520
00:36:25,911 --> 00:36:29,232
Welcome to Mickey Smith airlines,
please enjoy your flight!

521
00:36:37,251 --> 00:36:39,377
We did it! We did it!

522
00:36:44,398 --> 00:36:46,445
SHE SHRIEKS

523
00:37:03,408 --> 00:37:06,240
Pete! Take this!

524
00:37:07,526 --> 00:37:08,765
Use it!

525
00:37:08,805 --> 00:37:12,654
Hold the button down and press
it against the rope. Just do it!

526
00:37:14,882 --> 00:37:16,948
Jackie Tyler.

527
00:37:16,988 --> 00:37:18,949
This is for her.

528
00:37:30,964 --> 00:37:33,022
HE SCREAMS

529
00:38:13,286 --> 00:38:16,554
So, what happens inside that thing
then? Do you want to see?

530
00:38:16,594 --> 00:38:18,078
I don't think so.

531
00:38:19,836 --> 00:38:23,302
But you two,
all that stuff you said.

532
00:38:23,342 --> 00:38:25,155
About different worlds.

533
00:38:26,865 --> 00:38:28,377
Who are you?

534
00:38:30,138 --> 00:38:32,845
It's like you said.

535
00:38:32,885 --> 00:38:36,840
Imagine there are different worlds,

536
00:38:36,880 --> 00:38:38,556
parallel worlds.

537
00:38:38,596 --> 00:38:41,353
Worlds with another Pete Tyler.

538
00:38:42,840 --> 00:38:45,387
And Jackie Tyler, still alive.

539
00:38:45,427 --> 00:38:47,638
And their daughter.

540
00:38:50,747 --> 00:38:53,262
I've got to go.
But if you just look inside. . .

541
00:38:53,302 --> 00:38:58,608
I can't. There's all those
Lumic factories out there,
all those Cybermen in storage.

542
00:38:58,648 --> 00:39:01,973
Someone's got to tell
the authorities what happened.

543
00:39:03,805 --> 00:39:07,761
Rose, I've only got
five minutes of power.

544
00:39:07,801 --> 00:39:13,229
We've got to go.
The Doctor could show you.
Thank you. . .for everything.

545
00:39:13,269 --> 00:39:14,752
Dad. . .

546
00:39:16,824 --> 00:39:19,246
Don't. Just don't.

547
00:39:33,437 --> 00:39:35,892
Here it is.

548
00:39:37,390 --> 00:39:39,866
I found it, not a crease.

549
00:39:39,906 --> 00:39:43,021
My suit! Good man!

550
00:39:43,061 --> 00:39:46,215
Now then, Jake, we've got to run,
but one more thing.

551
00:39:46,255 --> 00:39:49,449
Mrs Moore.
Her real name was Angela Price.

552
00:39:49,489 --> 00:39:51,925
She's got a husband out there,
and children.

553
00:39:51,965 --> 00:39:55,400
Find them. Tell them how
she died saving the world.

554
00:39:55,440 --> 00:39:57,236
Yeah. Course I will.

555
00:39:57,276 --> 00:39:58,796
Off we go then.

556
00:39:58,836 --> 00:40:00,592
Um. . .

557
00:40:00,632 --> 00:40:02,149
Thing is, I'm staying.

558
00:40:02,189 --> 00:40:05,265
You're doing what?

559
00:40:05,305 --> 00:40:08,101
But you can't.
It sort of balances out.

560
00:40:08,141 --> 00:40:11,136
Cos this world lost its Ricky,
but there's me.

561
00:40:11,176 --> 00:40:14,573
And there's work to be done with
all those Cybermen still out there.

562
00:40:14,613 --> 00:40:17,730
But you can't stay.

563
00:40:17,770 --> 00:40:19,367
Rose, my gran's here.

564
00:40:21,397 --> 00:40:24,554
She's still alive.
My old gran, remember her? Yeah.

565
00:40:24,594 --> 00:40:27,030
She needs me.

566
00:40:27,070 --> 00:40:29,426
What about me, what if I need you?

567
00:40:29,466 --> 00:40:31,425
Yeah, but Rose,

568
00:40:31,465 --> 00:40:33,420
you don't.

569
00:40:33,460 --> 00:40:35,717
It's just you and him, isn't it?

570
00:40:38,971 --> 00:40:41,369
We had something
a long time ago, but. . .

571
00:40:41,409 --> 00:40:43,766
not any more.

572
00:40:43,806 --> 00:40:45,921
Well, we'll come back.

573
00:40:45,961 --> 00:40:48,438
We can travel anywhere!
Come and see you, yeah?

574
00:40:48,478 --> 00:40:49,961
We can't.

575
00:40:52,034 --> 00:40:55,748
I told you, travel between
parallel worlds is impossible.

576
00:40:55,788 --> 00:40:58,544
We got here by accident.
We fell through a crack in time.

577
00:40:58,584 --> 00:41:01,205
When we leave, I've got to close it.

578
00:41:03,452 --> 00:41:05,578
We can't ever return.

579
00:41:11,642 --> 00:41:13,859
Doctor.

580
00:41:14,158 --> 00:41:17,273
Take Rose's phone.
It's got the Code, get it out there,

581
00:41:17,313 --> 00:41:19,365
stop those factories.

582
00:41:21,505 --> 00:41:23,187
And good luck. . .

583
00:41:24,980 --> 00:41:28,016
Mickey the Idiot. Watch it!

584
00:41:41,114 --> 00:41:42,671
Thanks.

585
00:41:44,386 --> 00:41:46,945
We've had a laugh though,
haven't we?

586
00:41:46,985 --> 00:41:49,196
Seen it all. Been there and back.

587
00:41:51,816 --> 00:41:56,352
Who'd have thought
me and you off that old estate,
flying through the stars.

588
00:41:56,392 --> 00:41:58,558
All those years, just sitting there.

589
00:42:00,021 --> 00:42:03,535
Imagining what we'd do one day.

590
00:42:03,575 --> 00:42:05,957
We never saw this, did we?

591
00:42:13,802 --> 00:42:15,439
Go on. Don't miss your flight.

592
00:42:42,274 --> 00:42:44,730
Jake, you want to watch this.

593
00:42:48,906 --> 00:42:51,578
What the hell? !

594
00:42:51,618 --> 00:42:54,534
That's the Doctor. In the Tardis.

595
00:42:54,574 --> 00:42:56,546
With Rose Tyler.

596
00:43:04,040 --> 00:43:06,087
TARDIS PULSATES

597
00:43:11,108 --> 00:43:13,067
You're alive!

598
00:43:13,107 --> 00:43:15,142
Oh, Mum, you're alive!

599
00:43:15,181 --> 00:43:17,697
Well, I was the last time I looked.

600
00:43:17,737 --> 00:43:20,298
What is it?
What happened, sweetheart?

601
00:43:20,338 --> 00:43:22,730
What's wrong? Where did you go?

602
00:43:22,770 --> 00:43:28,158
Far away. That was. . .far away.

603
00:43:28,198 --> 00:43:30,784
Where's Mickey? He's gone home.

604
00:43:43,419 --> 00:43:46,813
I know it's not easy, with my
face looking exactly like Ricky.

605
00:43:46,853 --> 00:43:49,130
But I'm different,
I'm not replacing him.

606
00:43:49,170 --> 00:43:52,325
But we can remember him,
by fighting in his name.

607
00:43:54,200 --> 00:43:58,273
All those cyberfactories
out there, do you think
there'd be one in Paris?

608
00:43:58,313 --> 00:44:00,952
Yeah. Then let's go
and liberate Paris!

609
00:44:00,992 --> 00:44:03,533
What, you and me? In a van?

610
00:44:04,307 --> 00:44:06,260
Nothing wrong with a van!

611
00:44:06,300 --> 00:44:09,376
I once saved the universe
with a big yellow truck!

612
00:44:29,865 --> 00:44:32,859
There you go, sir.
All wired up for the grand occasion.

613
00:44:32,899 --> 00:44:34,826
WOMAN: Someone help me please!

614
00:44:34,856 --> 00:44:38,915
Ordinary people are being struck
down and changed and the only
new thing is a television.

615
00:44:47,793 --> 00:44:49,713
Men in black?

616
00:44:49,753 --> 00:44:51,310
Vanishing police cars?

617
00:44:51,350 --> 00:44:54,186
This is Churchill's England,
not Stalin's Russia!

618
00:44:54,225 --> 00:44:57,060
Are you sitting comfortably? Good.

619
00:44:57,100 --> 00:44:59,027
Then we'll begin.
